00:40:57.747 --> 00:40:59.857
"engage with concurrent movements

00:40:59.857 --> 00:41:02.477
"contesting Christian humanism at Yale,

00:41:02.477 --> 00:41:05.647
"specifically women's studies
and African American studies?

00:41:05.647 --> 00:41:07.257
"How would you characterize
the relationship

00:41:07.257 --> 00:41:09.210
"between these movements?"

00:41:09.210 --> 00:41:10.667
And then another one,

00:41:10.667 --> 00:41:13.957
"Must we conjoin humanism to Christianity?

00:41:13.957 --> 00:41:17.717
"Admittedly, it was so
conjoined at the Quattrocento,

00:41:17.717 --> 00:41:21.017
"but humanism now despised by Christianity

00:41:21.017 --> 00:41:23.717
"was the undergirding of
the scientific method.

00:41:23.717 --> 00:41:26.377
"The age of theory contained
a good deal of reaction

00:41:26.377 --> 00:41:29.930
"and posturing De Man, not
to mention obscurantism,"

00:41:29.930 --> 00:41:30.993
someone wrote in.

00:41:32.045 --> 00:41:34.350
- So these are great questions.

00:41:34.350 --> 00:41:37.880
I'll just start at the
first one, which I believe

00:41:37.880 --> 00:41:41.818
was about being uncomfortable
with the word anti-humanism,

00:41:41.818 --> 00:41:43.773
I think was the question.
- Yeah.

00:41:43.773 --> 00:41:46.370
- I would just argue,
I thought about this.

00:41:46.370 --> 00:41:50.510
I see this moment with this paper,

00:41:50.510 --> 00:41:55.440
and what I'm trying to talk
about as a dialectical in a way.

00:41:55.440 --> 00:41:58.367
I see, at the end of their careers,

00:42:00.821 --> 00:42:03.100
for example, Hartman and
Bloom are very comfortable

00:42:03.100 --> 00:42:05.965
saying I'm humanist,
I'm a humanist, right?

00:42:05.965 --> 00:42:10.710
Now, in the '70s, they are
labeled as anti-humanist,

00:42:10.710 --> 00:42:13.440
but I see it as dialectical
in that some of the moves

00:42:13.440 --> 00:42:15.950
that some of these scholars are making

00:42:15.950 --> 00:42:20.950
are in the name of a humanism,
but they are critiquing

00:42:21.210 --> 00:42:24.490
some of the assumptions
or implicit meanings

00:42:24.490 --> 00:42:28.870
that are then loaded with
humanism as it was practiced

00:42:28.870 --> 00:42:31.160
in the '50s, '60s, and '70s.

00:42:31.160 --> 00:42:35.330
So I see it as historical in that sense,

00:42:35.330 --> 00:42:38.710
and not like we could pick this work out

00:42:38.710 --> 00:42:41.380
of its historical context
to say, oh, anti-humanist.

00:42:41.380 --> 00:42:42.213
You know?

00:42:42.213 --> 00:42:44.250
It was in the name of a humanism,

00:42:44.250 --> 00:42:46.346
especially looking back on it,

00:42:46.346 --> 00:42:51.346
but it was sometimes labeled
itself as anti-humanist.

00:42:51.619 --> 00:42:55.560
But again, the dialectical,
these sort of movement,

00:42:55.560 --> 00:42:58.540
I think, is important,
and I had one sentence

00:42:58.540 --> 00:43:00.430
in the beginning of my
talk that I think kind

00:43:00.430 --> 00:43:03.980
of alludes to this argument,
and then I sort of moved on.

00:43:03.980 --> 00:43:05.763
So that's how I would answer that.

00:43:07.730 --> 00:43:10.695
So these are humanists,
but they are attacking

00:43:10.695 --> 00:43:14.490
the principles of humanism in
the name of a new humanism.

00:43:14.490 --> 00:43:19.490
Now, the De Man case, I think
that's more complicated,

00:43:21.185 --> 00:43:25.100
personally, I think that
that's, and I can't,

00:43:25.100 --> 00:43:26.946
I feel uncomfortable talking about it

00:43:26.946 --> 00:43:31.733
with this project that
I talked about today.

00:43:32.730 --> 00:43:37.730
Whether he's an anti-humanist
for all time is a debatable,

00:43:38.890 --> 00:43:42.293
is probably the case.

00:43:44.750 --> 00:43:46.320
So, and then the second question,

00:43:46.320 --> 00:43:47.170
I think was a Heidegger,

00:43:47.170 --> 00:43:48.357
is that a question about Heidegger?

00:43:48.357 --> 00:43:51.100
- Are there are Heideggerian connotations

00:43:51.100 --> 00:43:54.148
to anti-humanist-
- So, Heidegger,

00:43:54.148 --> 00:43:57.530
well, I mean, so speaking
of the two main figures

00:43:57.530 --> 00:43:58.860
I looked at, Bloom and Hartman,

00:43:58.860 --> 00:44:02.330
I mean, Bloom notoriously said,

00:44:02.330 --> 00:44:07.054
very, very, very funny, but
also aggressive comments

00:44:07.054 --> 00:44:08.890
