00:44:08.890 --> 00:44:11.640
and all the Heideggerian critics

00:44:11.640 --> 00:44:13.520
that were inspired by Heidegger,

00:44:13.520 --> 00:44:15.220
even though he was very close friends,

00:44:15.220 --> 00:44:17.620
Bloom was very close friends with Derrida

00:44:17.620 --> 00:44:19.490
and all these other figures.

00:44:19.490 --> 00:44:22.452
So is there something
suspiciously Heideggerian about?

00:44:22.452 --> 00:44:24.770
I mean, think, (clears throat)

00:44:24.770 --> 00:44:29.770
Heidegger does cast a
long, intellectual shadow

00:44:34.457 --> 00:44:38.720
that whether, for example,
in the case of Bloom,

00:44:38.720 --> 00:44:41.280
whether they agree with Heidegger or not,

00:44:41.280 --> 00:44:43.290
they were still struggling and dealing

00:44:43.290 --> 00:44:47.930
with what had been created in
the aftermath of Heidegger,

00:44:47.930 --> 00:44:51.360
and also, of course,
Heidegger's complicity

00:44:51.360 --> 00:44:53.990
with the Nazi regime and
what that all brings up

00:44:53.990 --> 00:44:57.750
and very serious, very,
very serious issues.

00:44:57.750 --> 00:45:01.210
So does it raise this Heidegger? Yes.

00:45:01.210 --> 00:45:02.260
I mean, I think that it does.

00:45:02.260 --> 00:45:07.260
I think in a larger study, this
would have to be addressed.

00:45:07.624 --> 00:45:08.874
And yes.
- Okay.

00:45:09.955 --> 00:45:10.788
Great.

00:45:10.788 --> 00:45:13.680
So I wanna dig down a little bit deeper

00:45:13.680 --> 00:45:18.680
