00:54:55.470 --> 00:55:00.330
about the current campus dynamics,

00:55:00.330 --> 00:55:05.330
and someone, one of the
people in the questions

00:55:05.860 --> 00:55:09.670
put it very well that Jews used to be seen

00:55:09.670 --> 00:55:13.893
as these kind of renegades,

00:55:16.020 --> 00:55:19.430
kind of challenging accepted norms,

00:55:19.430 --> 00:55:24.383
and now, arguably, are seen
as part of the establishment,

00:55:26.818 --> 00:55:30.860
kind of just white,
basically, at Yale now.

00:55:30.860 --> 00:55:34.940
And so, I don't know, can
you say something about that,

00:55:34.940 --> 00:55:37.573
and kind of current campus dynamics?

00:55:38.570 --> 00:55:40.070
Not at Yale, necessarily, but.

00:55:41.970 --> 00:55:45.210
- So that's really tough for me to answer,

00:55:45.210 --> 00:55:46.583
to be honest with you.

00:55:48.678 --> 00:55:50.720
I'm not sure how to answer that,

00:55:50.720 --> 00:55:55.630
and the reason why is
because I have lived in China

00:55:55.630 --> 00:55:58.727
since 2016, and I think that,

00:55:58.727 --> 00:56:03.023
I mean, I understand the question, but,

00:56:04.510 --> 00:56:06.380
I think it's a great question,

00:56:06.380 --> 00:56:11.200
how the switch from renegade
to, let's say, establishment,

00:56:11.200 --> 00:56:12.723
or I'm not sure how you wanna put it, but,

00:56:12.723 --> 00:56:13.743
when that happened.

00:56:17.390 --> 00:56:19.520
Oh gosh, I'm really sorry.

00:56:19.520 --> 00:56:22.133
- Yeah, no, no, no, I
mean, it's interesting-

00:56:23.168 --> 00:56:24.225
- [Gregory] Great question.

00:56:24.225 --> 00:56:27.178
- And you know, to kind
of think about the place

00:56:27.178 --> 00:56:32.178
of Judaic Studies, one
of the kind of goals,

00:56:33.336 --> 00:56:37.550
I think, of our program,
the antisemitism program,

00:56:37.550 --> 00:56:41.420
is to inject questions
of antisemitism and Jews

00:56:41.420 --> 00:56:44.660
into discussions about race on campus.

00:56:44.660 --> 00:56:48.403
And so, and to try to think
about ways to do that.

00:56:49.560 --> 00:56:52.180
Anyway, it's an interesting thing.

00:56:52.180 --> 00:56:54.910
So can you just say, so are you, really,

00:56:54.910 --> 00:56:57.560
last question, how are you
think about this project?

00:56:57.560 --> 00:57:01.520
Are you seeing it develop as a book?

00:57:01.520 --> 00:57:04.050
Is it like a group portrait?

00:57:04.050 --> 00:57:07.360
Is it gonna be focused on Yale
or was that talk just for us

00:57:07.360 --> 00:57:09.460
or how are you seeing it?

00:57:09.460 --> 00:57:10.513
- No, I mean,

00:57:12.063 --> 00:57:17.063
I have an idea for a project
about like global theory,

00:57:19.540 --> 00:57:24.540
its production at various
sites in the United States,

00:57:25.720 --> 00:57:30.720
and then its dissemination
abroad, and this would be,

00:57:32.120 --> 00:57:35.960
this was a project that
really got me really thinking

00:57:35.960 --> 00:57:38.733
about how and why that was happening,

00:57:39.710 --> 00:57:41.750
and so, for example,
my definition of theory

00:57:41.750 --> 00:57:44.163
at the beginning, trying to understand,

00:57:45.101 --> 00:57:48.180
these Jews, one way of thinking about it

00:57:48.180 --> 00:57:51.360
is they formalized the assumptions.

00:57:51.360 --> 00:57:53.010
Right, they used, these are techniques

00:57:53.010 --> 00:57:56.320
that formalized the ones,
the assumptions that existed

00:57:56.320 --> 00:57:57.570
in the culture around them.

00:57:57.570 --> 00:57:59.140
And whatever situation they were in,

00:57:59.140 --> 00:58:00.640
whatever field they were in,

00:58:00.640 --> 00:58:02.727
so I see this as part of a larger project,

00:58:02.727 --> 00:58:06.880
but it won't be focused on Yale,

00:58:06.880 --> 00:58:09.410
although I'm happy to continue.

00:58:09.410 --> 00:58:13.646
These were great questions,
and happy to expand this,

00:58:13.646 --> 00:58:15.670
but I guess we'll see.

00:58:15.670 --> 00:58:17.410
- Okay, terrific.

00:58:17.410 --> 00:58:20.860
Well thank you so much for
sharing your work with us,

00:58:20.860 --> 00:58:24.980
and thank you to everyone in the audience,

00:58:24.980 --> 00:58:26.440
and everyone who submitted questions,

00:58:26.440 --> 00:58:29.320
and as I said, I encourage everybody to go

00:58:29.320 --> 00:58:33.180
to the YPSA website and
sign up for our mailing list

00:58:33.180 --> 00:58:37.630
and we have a lot of other
great programs set up

00:58:37.630 --> 00:58:39.710
for this coming semester.

00:58:39.710 --> 00:58:41.414
So thanks to Greg.

00:58:41.414 --> 00:58:43.510
I will clap for everyone.

00:58:43.510 --> 00:58:46.539
You can't hear all the
clapping, but it's there,

00:58:46.539 --> 00:58:50.243
and see you all at another
event sometime soon.

00:58:51.140 --> 00:58:52.140
- Thank you so much.

